-- title:
--   Crossings of the two-chart model enumerated by k-points
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-th cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta \in L$, and the intermediate field $K$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the image under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137). Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ whose maximal ideal contains $p$ and whose image in $L$ contains $\zeta$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra which is a field of characteristic $p$. Let $c_1 : C_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ and $c_2 : C_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $i_1, i_2$ be closed immersions of $C_1, C_2$ into the fibre product of [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) with $\operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, each commuting with the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} k$, i.e. satisfying $i_\bullet \circ \mathrm{pr}_2 = c_\bullet$ in the sense of `SchemeHomOver`. Assume every point of that fibre product lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, that the scheme $C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2$ is reduced, and that its underlying set has cardinality $n$ with $n > 0$. Then there is a family $z : \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to \mathrm{Hom}(\operatorname{Spec} k, C_1 \times_{X_k} C_2)$ such that for each $i$ the composite of $z_i$ with $\mathrm{pr}_1$ followed by $c_1$ is the identity of $\operatorname{Spec} k$, likewise for $\mathrm{pr}_2$ followed by $c_2$, and the map sending $i$ to the image of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} k$ under $z_i$ is injective.
--
--   This is the enumeration step for the crossing locus of the two components of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over the valuation ring above $p$: the $n$ crossing points are realised, injectively, by $k$-valued points that are sections over both components. It is used in the construction of a rigidified line bundle on that model whose pullbacks along the components are prescribed tensor powers of the Poincaré bundle.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_fin_hom_pullback_comp_eq_id_and_injective_base_closedPoint_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

